omes due soon (maturity wall about 1.7 years out), so refinancing terms matter."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 38.1% over 3 years and 21.4% over 5 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 39%).","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 1.0% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 68.2% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+1.8% trend).","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.9x, 10.7% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 53, clearing the bar for a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.6%), and institutions hold 86%.","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 5 sales over the past year, net $1.8M sold.","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.3% (0.4% in dividends).","The share count has grown 31.8% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It has paid a dividend for 10 consecutive years."],"people":["With about 2,620 employees, each generates about $790K of revenue, 1.3x the Basic Materials median, and revenue has grown 9.7% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $254K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.4M (3x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $7K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":73,"head":"Watch: composite 49, above the 39 line, but the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread) and it earns less than its cost of capital.","pros":["Composite 49, above the 39 line (gates 11/25)","Trades 43% below fair value of $18.84","FCF margin 32.2%","Revenue grew 21.4%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA -0.6x"],"cons":["ROIC 1.0% vs WACC 11.4%","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)"],"flags":[],"need":["the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","it earns less than its cost of capital"],"buy_below":16.01,"vc":{"base":18.84,